842 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 673 0 R
/E (With sustainability integration emerging as directly linked to better financial outcomes and business performance \(54% of CEOs surveyed in a 2025 Bain & Company study tie sustainability directly to value creation\) and large corporates set, re-set, and adjust Scope 3 and supply chain emissions reduction strategies, SMEs are finding themselves under pressure to measure, report, and improve adequate sustainability performance.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
843 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 673 0 R
/E (The same Bain study also made clear a sharp shift on the buyer side: A significant share of B2B \(business-to-business\) buyers now intend to exclude suppliers that cannot demonstrate adequate sustainability performance  For SMEs, this poses a significant challenge, as large corporates and buyers typically represent opportunities for multi-year, recurring, contracts and revenue - though typical buyer criteria around sustainability performance data, tracking, and practices are aligned with guidance from frameworks and standards designed for larger, maturer, and less resourced-constrained entities. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
844 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 673 0 R
/E (This dynamic represents not only a potential barrier to SME supply chain participation, but also a broader missed opportunity to drive scalable sustainability integration, operational improvement, and decarbonization at scale across the segment responsible for a significant share of global economic activity and emissions.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
845 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 673 0 R
/E (Developed in partnership with the Society of Entrepreneurs and Ecology \(SEE\) Foundation, this report covers the development of a buyer-led sustainability rating system built on a pre-existing set of indicators designed for SEE, which were designed to drive sustainability adoption amongst SMEs. Rather than creating yet another set of performance and disclosure standards, which amount to subjective ratings depending on which components of sustainability are prioritized, this report introduces a different approach. The project proposes and delivers a system and AI-enabled tool that synthesize existing guidance into a decision-useful signal, built on a minimum viable dataset and comparable, industry-adjusted scoring. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
846 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 673 0 R
/T (SPRING 2026 CAPSTONE REPORT - SECTION 008)
/E (SPRING 2026 CAPSTONE REPORT - SECTION 008)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
