856 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 675 0 R
/T (Introduction)
/E (Introduction)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
857 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 675 0 R
/E (Existing sustainability ratings and disclosure frameworks - including third-party environmental, social, and governance \(ESG\) ratings such as EcoVadis, MSCI, and Sustainalytics, and leading reporting standards and frameworks like the Global Reporting Initiative \(GRI\), the Sustainability Accounting Standards Board \(SASB\), and the Task Force for Climate-Related Disclosures \(TCFD\) - were developed primarily to measure, or guide the disclosure of, sustainability performance for large, publicly listed global equities with investor-facing reporting obligations \(UNCTAD, 2024\). When applied to SMEs, these frameworks impose disproportionate costs and complexity. A global study of more than 16,000 SMEs found that 45% of U.S. SMEs describe environmental reporting standards as too complex, 43% cite high upfront costs as the primary barrier to action, and 63% report feeling pressure from customers to disclose sustainability progress \(Sage, 2023\). Without an SME-appropriate alternative, this misalignment risks excluding smaller firms from supply chains, restricting access to green finance, and concentrating sustainability progress among the largest market actors.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
858 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 675 0 R
/E (SEE is a preeminent Chinese organization that promotes environmental responsibility in business. With a nation-wide network of over 600 enterprises - the majority of which are SMEs - SEE identified the need for an innovative, clear, buyer-led sustainability engagement model that prompts practical SME participation without unreasonable reporting burdens or spend for headcount and oversight.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
859 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 675 0 R
/E (This project, developed in partnership with SEE, addresses this need by putting forth a framework and rating system designed specifically for SMEs. Critically, the framework is procurement-first and buyer-led, meaning it is designed to 1\) aid SMEs understand, identify, capture and present the sustainability information buyers are looking for, and 2\) allow buyers to quickly understand how suppliers and prospective suppliers align with their sustainability and business needs. The purpose of this rating is not to act as an all-in-one sustainability audit, but to serve as a viable tool to help SMEs make the sustainability decisions and disclosures that will have the greatest positive impact on their bottom lines - which serves as an incentive for practical sustainability adoption that SEE identified as critical for SME engagement.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
860 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 675 0 R
/E (This project aims to meet five interrelated objectives: )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
