/S /P
/P 678 0 R
/E (However, existing literature suggests that ESG ratings should not be treated as a single objective measure of sustainability performance \(Berg et al., 2022\). Studies highlight significant divergence among raters due to differences in scope, measurement, and weighting, alongside concerns about transparency and methodology \(IOSCO, 2021\). This has resulted in a growing discourse on the usefulness of ESG ratings in recent years, and raises the notion that comparing disclosures and ratings are distinct challenges. For practical applications, especially in SME contexts, the key takeaway is that clarity of objectives, transparent indicators, and clear explanation of scoring are more valuable than relying solely on complex, opaque rating systems)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
