>>
endobj
929 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 680 0 R
/E (Sustainability rating systems translate complex corporate behavior, practices, and data through several methodological approaches, and each have different implications for how organizations are assessed. The most widely-used methodology is materiality-adjusted weighting. Individual indicators are first scored with different categories \(such as environment, social, and governance\), and ultimately combined into a single composite score using predetermined category-level weights. Materiality-adjusted weights are differentiated by the industry sectors that have the different sustainability risks and opportunities \(EcoVadis, 2023\). Stakeholder-derived weights are determined through consultation with investors, civil society organizations, and other stakeholders, reflecting a deliberate choice about whose sustainability priorities should be privileged in the assessment.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
930 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 680 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
