/P 680 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
932 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 680 0 R
/E (Friede, Busch and Bassen \(2015\) found that controversy scores derived from media monitoring are significantly negatively correlated with financial performance, suggesting that they capture genuine sustainability risks rather than mere reputational noise. However, Drempetic, Klein and Zwergel \(2020\) found that larger companies receive more media coverage both positive and negative than smaller companies, regardless of their actual sustainability performance. This creates a systematic disadvantage for SMEs in assessment systems that rely heavily on external data sources, as their positive sustainability practices are less likely to be captured through media monitoring while their negative incidents, if any, may be disproportionately influenced relative to their actual impact.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
