/P 682 0 R
/E (Greenhouse gas emissions are one of the most important measurements for corporate environmental accountability. The Greenhouse Gas Protocol \(2015\) establishes the global standard for corporate GHG accounting, organizing emissions into three scopes: Scope 1 is cover direct emissions from company owned sources such as vehicles and boilers; Scope 2 captures indirect emissions from purchased electricity and heat; and Scope 3 encompasses all other indirect emissions across the value chain, including raw material extraction, transportation, and product end-of-life.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
