/P 683 0 R
/E (The United Nations Guiding Principles on Business and Human Rights \(United Nations, 2011\) expected that all companies should have a formal human rights policy commitment, a due diligence process for identifying and addressing human rights impacts, and a grievance mechanism through which affected stakeholders can seek remedy. Mares \(2012\) notes that while large multinational corporations have made significant progress in formalizing such policies, SMEs frequently lack the institutional capacity to develop and implement equivalent frameworks, creating a governance gap that sustainability assessment tools must be designed to address.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
