/P 689 0 R
/E (Section 3 describes the methodology, scoring logic, and system design used to develop the procurement-ready sustainability rating system for SMEs. The objective was not to create another exhaustive sustainability disclosure framework, but rather to operationalize sustainability into a practical, decision-useful tool capable of generating transparent scores and actionable recommendations for SMEs and their buyers.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
1014 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 689 0 R
/E (The methodology was therefore designed to identify which sustainability indicators are most relevant to SME procurement-readiness, determine how those indicators could be translated into measurable and repeatable questions, and develop a transparent scoring system capable of balancing cross-company comparability with industry- and market-specific context. At the same time, the system needed to preserve explainability while still leveraging AI-enabled functionality to generate tailored recommendations rather than static scores alone.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1015 0 obj
<<
