/S /P
/P 690 0 R
/E (First, the framework needed to be feasible for SMEs without dedicated sustainability teams, reporting infrastructure, or significant administrative capacity. Rather than replicating the breadth of large enterprise disclosure systems, the methodology focuses on a minimum viable dataset of indicators that are realistically measurable, repeatable over time, and useful within procurement and supplier evaluation contexts.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1026 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 690 0 R
/E (Second, the framework needed to be procurement-oriented rather than investor-oriented. Existing sustainability systems are often designed to support investor disclosure, regulatory compliance, or reputational risk management for large public corporations. However, the more immediate business driver for many SMEs is procurement: maintaining eligibility within supply chains and demonstrating alignment with buyer expectations. The methodology therefore prioritizes indicators that are material within supplier evaluation and operational sustainability contexts.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
