/P 696 0 R
/E (To accurately assess SME sustainability performance without overwhelming users, the team developed a relevant and minimal question set. Inputs such as industry, geography, target buyer, company size, and business goal determine which questions an SME receives in the evaluation.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
1119 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 696 0 R
/E (The methodology began with atomic decomposition. Sustainability frameworks and guidance documents were broken down into the smallest independent units of disclosure. Each atomic item represents a single measurable variable that can be reported, measured, and interpreted separately. This was necessary because many sustainability standards combine multiple concepts within a single disclosure requirement, such as reporting a metric, explaining a methodology, identifying governance responsibility, or describing a management process. While these concepts may be related, they are not interchangeable for scoring purposes and often require separate questions in the data intake process.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
1120 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 696 0 R
/E (Once extracted, the atomic indicators were analyzed across the knowledge base to identify repeated disclosure concepts. These concepts were grouped into clusters to consolidate overlapping requirements across frameworks and reduce duplicative information requests. Within each cluster, indicators were )
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
