1127 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 697 0 R
/E (Each question was mapped to a defined response type, such as boolean, percentage, numeric, categorical, date, or short-text input. This ensured that questions could support consistent data collection and scoring. Indicators that were overly open-ended, highly narrative, difficult to verify, or lacked a clear response structure were deprioritized. The goal was not to capture every possible sustainability issue, but to retain those indicators that could be answered by SMEs, repeated over time, and used to generate a meaningful sustainability signal for buyers.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1128 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 697 0 R
/E (This stage produced a reduced pool of disclosure items that were measurable, repeatable, feasible, and grounded in the knowledge base. The final result was a standardized question set designed to preserve cross-company comparability while still allowing for sector-specific materiality and procurement relevance.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1129 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 697 0 R
/E (The final question bank was designed as a deterministic, metadata-driven system. Each question is explicitly defined, rule-based, and traceable to source frameworks or guidance documents. The question bank includes metadata such as sustainability category, subcategory, response type, answer scale, industry applicability, geography applicability, buyer relevance, and trigger logic.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1130 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 697 0 R
/T (C. Question Generation & Trigger Logic )
/E (C. Question Generation & Trigger Logic )
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1131 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 697 0 R
/E (Importantly, question selection is deterministic rather than AI-generated. The system does not ask a language model to determine what questions an SME should answer. Instead, the tool relies on predefined rules and triggers to ensure consistency, explainability, and repeatability across assessments. Each question within the question bank includes metadata such as sustainability category, subcategory, response type, answer scale, industry applicability, geography applicability, buyer relevance, and trigger logic.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
1132 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 697 0 R
/E (The system applies layered trigger logic to determine which questions are presented to each SME. Universal questions apply across all users, while additional industry-, geography-, buyer-, and market-specific questions are selectively triggered depending on SME context.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
