/P 698 0 R
/E (Question selection occurs dynamically based on SME metadata inputs including industry, geography, target market, target buyer, company size, and business goals.The methodology is structured around a layered approach. The universal layer captures baseline disclosures that apply broadly across most SMEs and functions as the common denominator for cross-company comparison. The market layer captures regional or market-specific expectations. The industry layer captures sector-specific metrics tied to operational impacts and procurement relevance.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1137 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 698 0 R
/E (This layered structure was critical because sustainability risks and reporting priorities vary significantly by industry and market. A manufacturing SME, for example, may require more detailed questions on energy, emissions, waste, and chemical management, while a business services SME may face more relevant questions related to data privacy, cybersecurity, and governance practices.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1138 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 698 0 R
/E (For an SME sustainability score to be meaningful, responses to questions of fundamentally different types must be expressed in a common unit before they can be weighted and aggregated.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [3]
>>
