/Pg 42 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1214 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 703 0 R
/E (The AI agent receives four primary inputs: SME demographic and contextual information, questionnaire responses, scoring outputs, and relevant document excerpts retrieved from the knowledge base. Before recommendations are generated, the system performs a deterministic retrieval step that identifies the most relevant source documents and document chunks based on industry, geography, buyer context, sustainability category, and question-response alignment. This retrieval step constrains the AI system to a bounded and traceable subset of source materials rather than allowing unrestricted model-generated outputs.)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
1215 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 703 0 R
/E (The resulting recommendations are designed to be practical and operationally actionable. Outputs identify key sustainability gaps, procurement-relevant risks, improvement opportunities, and prioritized next steps. For example, a Manufacturing SME with limited hazardous waste tracking may receive recommendations related to formalized waste management procedures, supplier documentation practices, and operational controls aligned with buyer sustainability expectations.)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
1216 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 703 0 R
