1256 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 706 0 R
/T (This project delivers a carefully researched and constructed system designed to help accelerate sustainability adoption across SMEs. However, any scoring system built on synthesized guidance carries assumptions worth surfacing, and any tool intended for real-world use needs a credible path to adoption. The current methodology has vulnerabilities that would benefit from further hardening, and getting the tool into the hands of SMEs, buyers, and institutions will require deliberate sequencing and framing.)
/E (This project delivers a carefully researched and constructed system designed to help accelerate sustainability adoption across SMEs. However, any scoring system built on synthesized guidance carries assumptions worth surfacing, and any tool intended for real-world use needs a credible path to adoption. The current methodology has vulnerabilities that would benefit from further hardening, and getting the tool into the hands of SMEs, buyers, and institutions will require deliberate sequencing and framing.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1257 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 706 0 R
/T (A. Methodological Limitations and Sources of Variability)
/E (A. Methodological Limitations and Sources of Variability)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1258 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 706 0 R
/E (1. Clustering involves subjective judgment. Even with explicit rules, deciding whether to group indicators into one cluster or two requires analyst judgment. Different people applying the same rules may produce different cluster maps. Future versions should measure this using inter-rater reliability metrics like Cohen's kappa \(Landis & Koch, 1977\).)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1259 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 706 0 R
/E (2. Frequency is not the same as materiality. Weights reflect what appears often in the corpus, not what matters most in the real world. The corpus over-represents frameworks favored by large enterprise buyers \(GHG Protocol, GRI, CDP, CSRD\) and under-represents emerging standards, Global South frameworks, and sector-specific standards outside the five covered sectors. An issue critical to, say, Bangladeshi textiles may be underweighted simply because the relevant documents aren't yet included.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1260 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 706 0 R
/E (3. Multipliers need ongoing maintenance. Tag- and cluster-based rules are extensible but require regular review. As regulations evolve \(e.g., UK SDR enactment, Brazilian TNFD-aligned rules, Singapore carbon tax changes\), multipliers must be updated. Without a scheduled review process, this layer will drift out of sync with actual buyer and regulatory expectations.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1261 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 706 0 R
/E (4. The corpus has gaps. The ~70 documents are substantial but incomplete. Notable omissions include TNFD, the Social Value Act guidance, EU Taxonomy technical screening criteria, and most SASB standards outside the five sectors. Concepts central to these frameworks, especially nature-related financial risk, are likely underweighted.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
