/T (5. AI outputs vary between runs. Atomic extraction, clustering, and question generation all rely on language model inference, which is probabilistic. Different model versions, temperatures, or prompts can yield different results. Rule-bound prompts and correction passes reduce this, but no formal variability study has been done yet. This matters most at the clustering stage, where small differences shift frequency counts and therefore every downstream weight.)
/E (5. AI outputs vary between runs. Atomic extraction, clustering, and question generation all rely on language model inference, which is probabilistic. Different model versions, temperatures, or prompts can yield different results. Rule-bound prompts and correction passes reduce this, but no formal variability study has been done yet. This matters most at the clustering stage, where small differences shift frequency counts and therefore every downstream weight.)
/Pg 46 0 R
