1292 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 709 0 R
/E (This project set out to address a structural mismatch within the sustainability landscape: the frameworks, disclosure systems, and ratings that increasingly shape supply chain access and procurement decisions were largely designed for large, well-resourced corporations, while many of the businesses now expected to comply with them are SMEs operating with significantly fewer financial, technical, and reporting resources. Rather than introducing another comprehensive framework into an already fragmented sustainability ecosystem, the system developed in partnership with the Society of Entrepreneurs & Ecology \(SEE\) Foundation synthesizes existing disclosure expectations into a streamlined, procurement-ready sustainability signal calibrated to the operational realities of SMEs and the contexts in which they compete.)
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1293 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 709 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1294 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 709 0 R
/E (At its core, this project reframes sustainability assessment from a purely disclosure-oriented exercise into a practical business and procurement tool. The framework prioritizes transparency, comparability, usability, and actionability by combining deterministic scoring methodologies with AI-enabled, source-grounded recommendations tailored to each SME user. In doing so, the system attempts to address a longstanding limitation within conventional ESG ratings and disclosure systems: the gap between assessment and implementation.)
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
