1301 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 710 0 R
/E (Procurement-ready sustainability therefore offers one practical mechanism for turning buyer pressure into scalable sustainability adoption. For SMEs, it can make sustainability more legible, feasible, and commercially relevant. For buyers, it can create a clearer basis for assessing suppliers, prioritizing sustainability preferences, and engaging smaller businesses before excluding them from supply chains. For the broader economy, it offers a pathway to extend sustainability infrastructure beyond large corporations and into the segment that represents the majority of global businesses, employment, and supply chain activity. While the system developed through this project remains a minimum viable product rather than a finalized global standard, it demonstrates how transparent scoring, curated sustainability guidance, and AI-enabled recommendations can be combined to lower reporting burden, improve procurement decision-making, and accelerate a more inclusive transition toward a sustainable global economy.)
/Pg 49 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
