2178 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 745 0 R
/E (This formula gives a score of 100 when x = 0 \(no adverse events\), 50 when x = 1, 33 when x = 2, and so on, declining asymptotically toward zero as the count increases. The function has the desirable property that it penalises the first adverse event most heavily, consistent with the procurement expectation that any instance of a serious safety violation or regulatory fine is a significant negative signal. Meanwhile, it treats additional events with progressively less marginal impact, reflecting the reality that a company with 10 incidents is not ten times worse than one with 1 incident from a supplier qualification perspective.)
/Pg 84 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
