2197 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 747 0 R
/E (Conversely, consistently low working hours relative to a full-time standard may indicate underemployment, precarious labor arrangements, or a workforce that is not truly engaged with the company, also signaling concern to buyers assessing the stability and reliability of their supply base.)
/Pg 86 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
2198 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 747 0 R
/E (The appropriate normalization for this metric is therefore Gaussian \(bell-curve\) shaped, centered on the target value that represents the socially optimal working week. The formula is:)
/Pg 86 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
2199 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 747 0 R
/E <6E6F726D616C697A65645F73636F7265203D20657870288A302E3520D720282878208A20706172616D5F3129202F20706172616D5F3229322920D720313030>
/Pg 86 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
2200 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 747 0 R
/E (where param_1 is the target \(optimal\) working hours per week, and param_2 is the standard deviation controlling how quickly the score declines as hours deviate from the target in either direction. A company reporting working hours exactly equal to param_1 receives a score of 100. A company reporting hours one standard deviation above or below the target receives a score of approximately 61. Two standard deviations above or below receive approximately 14. This penalises both overwork and underemployment in a symmetric and continuous way, without imposing a binary threshold that would categorize any specific number of hours as categorically acceptable or unacceptable.)
/Pg 86 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
2201 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 747 0 R
/E (The Gaussian normalization method is well established in environmental performance assessment for metrics where the optimal value lies in an interior range rather than at an extreme \(van der Werf & Petit, 2002\). Its use here for working hours reflects the broader design principle that normalization methods should match the underlying empirical relationship between the raw metric and the sustainability outcome it is intended to capture, rather than imposing a uniform directional logic across all questions.)
/Pg 86 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
