2326 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 753 0 R
/T (Some disclosure concepts are inherently more material for certain sectors due to the nature of their operations and the expectations of their buyer communities. The theoretical foundation for this is the sector-differentiated materiality framework described by Khan, Serafeim, and Yoon \(2016\), who demonstrate that financially material sustainability issues differ significantly across industries: environmental metrics dominate in resource-intensive sectors; social and governance metrics dominate in knowledge-economy sectors. For example:)
/E (Some disclosure concepts are inherently more material for certain sectors due to the nature of their operations and the expectations of their buyer communities. The theoretical foundation for this is the sector-differentiated materiality framework described by Khan, Serafeim, and Yoon \(2016\), who demonstrate that financially material sustainability issues differ significantly across industries: environmental metrics dominate in resource-intensive sectors; social and governance metrics dominate in knowledge-economy sectors. For example:)
/Pg 92 0 R
/K [3]
>>
