6511 0 obj
<<
/Title (Where a legal or regulatory requirement imposes a disclosure obligation that exceeds the corpus-wide baseline, questions in the relevant cluster receive an upward multiplier. The EU CSRD, for example, mandates double materiality assessments, Scope 1/2/3 GHG disclosure, biodiversity impact assessment, and gender pay gap reporting for in-scope companies. SMEs supplying to EU enterprise buyers face significant indirect pressure to align with these requirements, as their buyers must in turn disclose their value chain impacts under CSRD. Questions in the G-RISK, P-DEI, R-WAT-WITHDRAW, and R-BIO clusters therefore carry higher multipliers for EU-market SMEs than the global average weight would suggest. This is consistent with empirical evidence that mandatory sustainability reporting requirements produce stronger and more consistent changes in corporate practice than voluntary frameworks \(Ioannou & Serafeim, 2017\), justifying a systematic upward adjustment for concepts mandated by law in the relevant jurisdiction.)
/Dest [92 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 6515 0 R
/Next 6507 0 R
>>
endobj
